The Arix wake module is original work, independently rewritten from scratch, and
is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only (see the LICENSE
file in this directory). The current sources carry no third-party GPL/LGPL code.

An earlier iteration of this module did contain four files derived from Operit
(LGPL-3.0-or-later). Those files were deleted outright, and the module was rebuilt
around a different architecture -- a VAD/MFCC front end feeding a switchable
decision stage (fixed-phrase KWS, or embedding-prototype matching for user-recorded
phrases), rather than the original MFCC+DTW listener. See DESIGN-WAKE.md.

This is an independent rewrite, not a "clean-room" reimplementation in the strict
sense of the term: the rewrite was done by the same author who had previously worked
on the derived files, not by a separate team walled off from the original. The
distinction is worth stating plainly, because it costs nothing to admit -- Operit is
LGPL-3.0-**or-later**, which can be taken under GPL-3.0 and is therefore compatible
with this project's AGPL-3.0 anyway.

Note on the licence change: this module was previously Apache-2.0. The rewrite was
done to make Arix an independent project -- referencing others' ideas rather than
carrying their code -- not in order to adopt a permissive licence. That goal is
unaffected by the project moving to AGPL-3.0, so the provenance statement above
stands unchanged.

